The following files should be included in your Guess Again! package:

      DOOR10         <-- the main program
      GUESS.DOC      <-- this documentation
      FICTIONAL.DAT  <-- text file of fictional character puzzles
      PERSON.DAT     <-- text file of person puzzles
      PHRASE.DAT     <-- text file of phrase puzzles
      PLACE.DAT      <-- text file of place puzzles
      TITLE.DAT      <-- text file of title puzzles
 
Also, the file GUESS.SCR will be created after playing.  It contains the top
ten scores.



                            P U Z Z L E    F I L E S

Each puzzle takes one line in the puzzle file.  They should be done in all
capital letters.  Anything that is not a captial letter (A-Z) will be shown
to the player.  So, a title such as "FRIDAY THE 13th" would appear to the
player as:                           ______ ___ 13th



                             I N F O R M A T I O N

Guess Again! was written by Mark D. Turner.  I've always wondered if a
shareware author asked for really low donations if he'd get anything.  So,
I'm calling this program Next-To-Nothing-Ware.  Use if forever and ever with
no strings attached.  But, if you think it's slightly worthwhile (or better),
then pop 25 cents or so into the mail to:

  Mark D. Turner
  P.O. Box 64
  Bluefield, VA 24605

You'll never miss the money and if only 100 people send it in, I'll have $25
to encourage the development of future freebies.  Go ahead, surprise me, and
mail something to me (wow, a dollar would probably send me to the hospital)!

I also run a part-time bbs, called The Outer Limits.  Currently, it runs from
8:00 am to 7:00 pm from Monday-Friday.  Frequently, it's on until 10:00 pm
and weekends, too.  Any problems can be reported to me there.  The number is
304-327-7452.  Yeah, that's right, it's a West Virginia number, even though
the mailing address is in Virginia.  We're right at the state line and the
story isn't anything you'd care to hear.

I hope you find Guess Again! of use.  I'm also working on a couple of other
doors, which I hope to release soon.

Have fun (or whatever else turns you on)!

Thanks to Percy Broadnax for creating Metro-BBS and the door routines.
